  "notes": "A keys-and-console model, and the research is unusually explicit about what he does *not* do: he did not program the drums. The documented division was kick/snare/hat from the lead producer, keys and bass from him — so this entry deliberately inherits its kit from the g-funk parent and overrides only the fill band, and that inheritance is the finding rather than a gap. What it does own is harmony and low end. Church-organ and piano training gives functional, full voicings, which is `extensions` at a quarter triad and a quarter ninth with a wide open register and stepwise top voice — the densest chord block on this axis. The Moog bass was played by hand when a session bassist could not deliver, so `humanize.quantizeStrength` drops to 0.7 and `bassline.glideProb` goes to 0.88 for the portamento between roots. ⚠ The research gives that bass as E1–C2, an 8-semitone window. The register here is [28,46] because a range that narrow gives the bass generator no reachable pool and `bass.rs` measures distinctness over it; E1 is still the floor and the top is the widening, not a reading of the record. ⚠ He introduced SSL automation to the lane and the research says that is *why* these records transition on moving mutes and layer entries rather than drum fills — so `drums.fills.fillBeforeSection` is false and `arrangement.transitions.switchUpProb` is raised instead. `high` is the research's own rating.",
